   "html_text": "Tessler and Goodman (2019) offer an account of generics that is rooted in a Bayesian computational approach to cognition. They model acceptance/rejection of a generic as a speaker’s decision to produce an utterance of the generic to a naive listener. The goal of the speaker, on their model, is to produce an utterance that aligns the listener’s beliefs about the prevalence of the property among members of the kind (the “referent prevalence” in their terminology) with the speaker’s beliefs. The sp",
